-Owner skill: `skill://ipc-contract`. Thin Tauri shell over `yamt_session::MergeSession` and `yamt_lsp_host::Host`, or with `--diff` over `yamt_compare::TabStore` (plan §2 #93–#97, #101), or with `--diff=<range>` over `yamt_range::Range` (plan §2 #103–#107): `lib.rs` (`run`, `export_bindings`) shared by both bins; `graphics.rs` (NVIDIA guard: the first statement of `run()`, the project's one `unsafe` line, plan §2 #43), `args.rs` (`yamt [--repo <path>]` → `Merge`, `yamt --diff` → `Compare`, `yamt --diff=<a>..<b>`/`--diff=<a>...<b>` with `--repo <path>` in either order → `Range { spec, repo }` through `RangeSpec::parse`, whose error is the usage line; `--diff` with `--repo` is a usage error, so is `--diff` with a `--diff=` or a second `--diff=` ("give --diff or one --diff=<range>, not both"); `--help`/`--version` win), `appimage.rs` (inside an AppImage — `APPIMAGE` and `APPDIR` set and the binary under `$APPDIR` — a relative `--repo` is resolved against `OWD`; never chdir, WebKit's helper paths are relative to `$APPDIR/usr`; called for `Merge` and `Range`, never for `Compare`), `outcome.rs` (start-up decision, exit status 0/1/2; the close ending, `ending_when_git_is_done` — `ending_on_close` once `lock_when_git_is_done` lets go: `Finished(kind)` 0 with `<operation> finished`, `Aborted(kind)` 1 with `<operation> aborted` (`merge aborted` for a merge), reading and writing nothing; `Held` lists through `refresh_stop` and counts git's view, a `MovedOn` there counting the stop git moved on to like `MovedOn`; `MovedOn` opens the stop git is at only to count its unmerged files, settling nothing), `merge.rs` (`Merge` = `Held(Box<MergeSession>)` | `Running(kind)` | `MovedOn { root, highest_disk_version }` | `Aborted(kind)` | `Finished(kind)`, the app's merge state as `MergeState` = `Mutex<Merge>`; `session()` answers `GitRunning`, `StopMovedOn`, `MergeAborted` or `MergeFinished` outside `Held` — the one state → refusal mapping, also what a worker hand-over refuses with; `has_