_dir>/yamt/range/` before listing (another window on the same pair: one line naming both short ids, exit 2), manages `RangeState { range, _lock }` without a `Mutex` (nothing changes after start), opens the window titled `<range as typed> — <repository folder> — yamt` and ends with exit 0 and no message at close; never a `MergeSession`, `HostState` or `TabStore`; the two commands `open_range` (`Range::start`) and `load_range_file` (`Range::load` on a `spawn_blocking` worker, a panic → `WorkerStopped`)), `clipboard.rs` (`read_clipboard(selection: ClipboardSelection)` → the text or `None`, for every window, no managed state, plan §2 #99: on Linux GTK's text request (`gtk::Clipboard::request_text`), started on the main thread by `run_on_main_thread` and waited for on a `spawn_blocking` worker, so a hung owner never blocks the window; it never asks GTK for the selection's format list — no `request_targets`, `wait_for_targets`, `wait_is_*_available`, `wait_for_contents`, `request_contents` — since WebKitGTK 2.54 crashes on a failed one; other systems answer `None`), `window.rs` (one window per run, merge, compare or range, built by one `open_and_wait` (`pub(crate)` with `context()` and `window_title`, for `range.rs`): reads `stored_at_start` once — theme and antialiasing — and applies font rendering before building the webview; the start script sets `<html data-theme>` and `<html data-window="merge|compare|range">` before the first frame; close fallback: a close request between `UNANSWERED_CLOSE_GRACE` and `UNANSWERED_CLOSE_TIMEOUT` after an unanswered one destroys the window; after the event loop the merge window runs `stop_all` so no language server outlives a normal close, then the ending once git is done; the compare window, titled `Compare — yamt`, never opens a `MergeSession`, runs git or manages `Mutex<Merge>`/`HostState`, and ends with exit 0 and no message), `font_rendering.rs` (Linux: the Antialiasing setting onto GTK's `gtk-xft-antialias`/`gtk-xft-rgba` before 